title: 2025 / 11 / 04 / श्लोकार्थः

अस्त्रेणेति ।मदस्त्रस्यामोघत्वात्तेन बन्धनमात्रं चतुःपञ्चघटिकानन्तरं पुनर्मोक्षश्चेति ब्रह्मदत्तवरात्‌ ।तावता कालेन ब्रह्मास्त्रमुक्तमात्मानं ज्ञात्वापि यदृच्छया कार्यान्तरप्रसङ्गेन रावणदर्शनापेक्षया ।यन्त्रिणो बद्ध्वा नेतॄंस्तान्राक्षसान्प्रति वीरो हन्तुं समर्थोऽपि मर्षयनक्षमां कुर्वन्‌। रावणसमीपं प्राप्तवानिति शेषः ।ममर्ष इति वा पाठः ॥ इति तिलकः 

This refers to the Astra (weapon).


<<<
(It is said) that due to the infallibility (unfailing nature) of the Astra (Brahmāstra), the bondage (caused by it) would last only for four or five ghaṭikās (approx. 1.5 to 2 hours), and thereafter there would be release—this was due to a boon given by Brahmā.

Although he knew that he would be released from the Brahmāstra within that time, (Hanumān did not wait for the release) but due to a desire to accomplish another task (i.e., meet Rāvaṇa) by his own will (yadr̥cchayā).

The brave (Hanumān), though capable of killing those Rākṣasas (demons) who were binding and leading him, pretended not to be capable (of resistance).

The rest of the story is that he reached Rāvaṇa's vicinity. (The reading could also be) mamarṣa (he tolerated/endured).
<<<


---
;सार-रूपेण (In Summary)

>The text explains that Hanumān allowed himself to be bound by Indrajit's Brahmāstra, knowing that the bondage would only last for a short time (about an hour and a half) due to a specific boon from Brahmā about the Astra's effect. However, Hanumān didn't wait for the automatic release. He intentionally tolerated the binding and pretended to be incapable of fighting back, as his primary motive was to use the opportunity to meet and observe Rāvaṇa.

